{"parentUuid":"d7d05e12-0b83-448b-a447-e9637cfb4dc2","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a0ac44e2d03f4edb2","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Ep1YVfMegVorDzv46nMDC7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XX6Tmzn718dZgcedLJCbPY","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html","prompt":"Extract patterns for: warm-starting / hint usage from previous solve, multi-stage solving with progressive gap tightening, callback-based mid-solve adjustments, and any anytime algorithm patterns. Include exact code snippets if available."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2614,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3202,"cache_read_input_tokens":21149,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3202,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caox6i43VLatnvfJgZUne","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"e11e8095-38e2-4fdf-a94c-87a9b68d3073","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:03.789Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e11e8095-38e2-4fdf-a94c-87a9b68d3073","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a0ac44e2d03f4edb2","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Ep1YVfMegVorDzv46nMDC7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VXbpx2GK9R54ACb7XCtLHo","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"CP-SAT solution_callback stop_search relative_gap incumbent dynamic adjustment"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2614,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3202,"cache_read_input_tokens":21149,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3202,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caox6i43VLatnvfJgZUne","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"1b08cec3-3dc2-4ee9-9df9-837cd9b327ef","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:04.577Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1b08cec3-3dc2-4ee9-9df9-837cd9b327ef","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a0ac44e2d03f4edb2","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Ep1YVfMegVorDzv46nMDC7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HZ2BAsV7wMDKf5cQHZoBdw","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"Gurobi callback set MIPGap dynamic SetParam during optimization GAP_TIGHTEN"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2614,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3202,"cache_read_input_tokens":21149,"output_tokens":589,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3202},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2614,"output_tokens":589,"cache_read_input_tokens":21149,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3202,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3202,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011Caox6i43VLatnvfJgZUne","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"6df129ad-bd7a-41d2-a9a2-0cd6146337f2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:05.634Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d7d05e12-0b83-448b-a447-e9637cfb4dc2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a0ac44e2d03f4edb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NwAk63msdwNP79eHkWjtdB","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Solver Parameters Summary\n\n## Time Limiting & Gap Control\n\n**max_time_in_seconds**\n- Used to prevent indefinite solver runtime on complex models\n- Example: `solver.parameters.max_time_in_seconds = 60`\n- Default value not explicitly stated in document\n\n**relative_gap_limit**\n- Stops solver when solution is within specified ratio of proven bound\n- Example: `solver.parameters.relative_gap_limit = 0.05` (5% of optimum)\n- Default value not explicitly stated\n\n**absolute_gap_limit**\n- Halts solving when solution is within specified absolute value of bound\n- Default value not explicitly stated\n- Mentioned alongside relative_gap_limit but no usage example provided\n\n## Parallelization\n\n**num_workers**\n- Controls number of CPU cores used for parallel solving\n- Example: `solver.parameters.num_workers = 8`\n- Default: \"all available cores (including hyperthreading)\"\n- Document notes reducing workers sometimes improves performance\n\n## Logging & Progress Tracking\n\n**log_search_progress**\n- Enables detailed solver progress logging during optimization\n- Example: `solver.parameters.log_search_progress = True`\n- Recommended for development to understand solver behavior\n\n## Solution Hints & Initialization\n\n**fix_variables_to_their_hinted_value**\n- Forces solver to use exact hinted variable values\n- Example: `solver.parameters.fix_variables_to_their_hinted_value = True`\n- Useful for testing hint feasibility\n\n**hint_conflict_limit**\n- Controls `debug_crash_on_bad_hint` triggering threshold (default: 10)\n- Document notes this feature is \"unreliable\"\n\n## Early Termination Options\n\nThe document describes multiple approaches beyond simple timeouts:\n- Solution callbacks via `CpSolverSolutionCallback.on_solution_callback()`\n- Bound callbacks via `solver.best_bound_callback`\n- Relative and absolute gap limits (noted above)"}]},"uuid":"1b22e875-9f06-4c7f-b568-3abd88cfd262","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:09.414Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d7d05e12-0b83-448b-a447-e9637cfb4dc2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"e11e8095-38e2-4fdf-a94c-87a9b68d3073","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a0ac44e2d03f4edb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XX6Tmzn718dZgcedLJCbPY","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Solver Patterns: Advanced Solving Techniques\n\n## Warm-Starting with Solution Hints\n\nThe primer demonstrates leveraging previous solutions as starting points for subsequent solves. When adding constraints that don't fundamentally alter the problem, warm-starting can significantly accelerate solving.\n\n**Key implementation details:**\n- Extract the current solution and add it as a hint to the model via `model.add_hint(variable, value)`\n- Enable hint repair with `solver.parameters.repair_hint = True`\n- Control repair effort using `solver.parameters.hint_conflict_limit` (e.g., value of 20)\n\nThe example shows this pattern when iteratively adding constraints like \"prohibit_combination\" after presenting initial solutions to users. The solver can attempt to repair the previous solution rather than starting from scratch.\n\n## Multi-Stage Solving with Progressive Objective Tightening\n\nThe \"Exchangeable Objective / Multi-Objective Optimization\" section illustrates sequential solving phases:\n\n1. **Phase 1:** Maximize primary objective (value)\n2. **Phase 2:** Fix previous objective to a relaxed bound (e.g., 95% of optimal), then minimize secondary objective (weight)\n\n**Critical pattern:** Use `fix_current_objective(ratio)` to constrain the prior objective while changing the goal function. A ratio of 0.95 permits 5% degradation in the original objective while exploring alternatives.\n\n## Callback-Based Mid-Solve Adjustments\n\nThe primer acknowledges callbacks enable progress updates but notes a limitation: \"the callback is not always called frequently, this may lead to problematic delays, making it unsuitable for graphical user interfaces.\"\n\n**Alternative architecture:** Run CP-SAT in a separate process using Python's `multiprocessing` module, communicating via pipes. This permits interruption at any time without waiting for callback invocation.\n\n## Anytime Algorithm Pattern\n\nThe embedded application example demonstrates responsive solver interaction through process isolation. The solver executes independently while the main application remains responsive to user interrupts—essential for interactive optimization interfaces.\n\nThe primer does not detail explicit callback-based mid-solve constraint modifications; instead, it advocates architectural separation for responsive systems."}]},"uuid":"1bf07b94-2165-4d3d-b82b-a284f6c0f36c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:11.181Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e11e8095-38e2-4fdf-a94c-87a9b68d3073","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1b08cec3-3dc2-4ee9-9df9-837cd9b327ef","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a0ac44e2d03f4edb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VXbpx2GK9R54ACb7XCtLHo","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT solution_callback stop_search relative_gap incumbent dynamic adjustment\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Setting solver limits | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_tasks\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"MIP Relative Optimality Tolerance | AIMMS Community\",\"url\":\"https://community.aimms.com/aimms-language-12/mip-relative-optimality-tolerance-405\"},{\"title\":\"Coding Patterns - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html\"},{\"title\":\"Obtaining Intermediate Solutions in OR-Tools CP-SAT [Fixed]\",\"url\":\"https://www.technetexperts.com/ortools-intermediate-solutions-callback/\"},{\"title\":\"A practical introduction to Constraint Programming using CP-SAT and Python\",\"url\":\"https://pganalyze.com/blog/a-practical-introduction-to-constraint-programming-using-cp-sat\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: com.google.ortools.sat.CpSolver Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/java/classcom_1_1google_1_1ortools_1_1sat_1_1CpSolver.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about CP-SAT's solution callback, stop_search, relative_gap, and dynamic adjustment features:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**Solution Callbacks:**\nThe CP-SAT solver provides a callback interface designed to monitor the search process. Understanding how to correctly implement this interface is critical for tracking progress, logging metrics, or storing suboptimal but feasible results that satisfy all constraints before the global optimum is identified.\n\n**Stopping Search:**\nSolution callbacks can be used to halt the solver, and you can make the solver terminate after it finds a specified number of solutions, as illustrated by examples showing how to stop the search after five solutions.\n\n**Relative Gap:**\nThe relative limit stops the solver when the objective value (O) is within a specified ratio of the bound (B). You can set the solver optimality tolerance using `solver.parameters.relative_gap_limit`.\n\n**Incumbent Solutions:**\nWhen solving an optimization problem with an objective function, the CP-SAT solver internally adds a dynamic constraint. Every time a solution is found, the solver ensures that any subsequent solution must strictly improve the objective value. Consequently, the default on_solution_callback method is only triggered when a better solution is discovered.\n\n**Dynamic Adjustment:**\nCP-SAT creates a dynamic, adaptive search strategy that responds to what the solver is learning. The solver periodically abandons the current search tree and starts over with a different variable ordering.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0f0cbfd2-02c1-4844-aa53-95eb976e391e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:12.301Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"1b08cec3-3dc2-4ee9-9df9-837cd9b327ef","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6df129ad-bd7a-41d2-a9a2-0cd6146337f2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a0ac44e2d03f4edb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HZ2BAsV7wMDKf5cQHZoBdw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Gurobi callback set MIPGap dynamic SetParam during optimization GAP_TIGHTEN\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parameter Reference - Gurobi Optimizer Reference Manual\",\"url\":\"https://docs.gurobi.com/projects/optimizer/en/current/reference/parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"What is the MIPGap? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/8265539575953-What-is-the-MIPGap\"},{\"title\":\"Parameter Guidelines - Gurobi Optimizer Reference Manual\",\"url\":\"https://docs.gurobi.com/projects/optimizer/en/current/concepts/parameters/guidelines.html\"},{\"title\":\"Why does MIPGap not give me the actual optimality gap? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/16159579824273-Why-does-MIPGap-not-give-me-the-actual-optimality-gap\"},{\"title\":\"How do I change parameters in a callback? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/360039233191-How-do-I-change-parameters-in-a-callback\"},{\"title\":\"Get MIPGap in Gurobi callbacks JuMP 0.21 - Optimization (Mathematical) - Julia Programming Language\",\"url\":\"https://discourse.julialang.org/t/get-mipgap-in-gurobi-callbacks-jump-0-21/37232\"},{\"title\":\"Multiple Objectives: MIPGap of each objective – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/360048036491-Multiple-Objectives-MIPGap-of-each-objective\"},{\"title\":\"How do I set multiple termination criteria for a model? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/360013419411-How-do-I-set-multiple-termination-criteria-for-a-model\"},{\"title\":\"How to control MIP using callbacks in multi-objective optimization – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/31513741528593-How-to-control-MIP-using-callbacks-in-multi-objective-optimization\"},{\"title\":\"How do I use callbacks to terminate the solver? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/360047717291-How-do-I-use-callbacks-to-terminate-the-solver\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding your query about Gurobi callbacks, MIPGap, and dynamic parameter changes during optimization:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**Changing Parameters in Callbacks:**\n\nFor Gurobi versions < 12.0.0, to change parameters within a callback you should terminate the optimization process in the callback, then set the parameter outside the callback, and call optimize() again. An example shows changing MIPGap after 4 seconds by detecting when a certain condition is met, setting a flag, and then changing the MIPGap parameter after terminating and re-optimizing.\n\n**Parameter Behavior:**\n\nParameters control the solver's behavior and are not changed during the optimization process. This means you cannot directly modify parameters like MIPGap while optimization is actively running—you must terminate and restart.\n\n**Important Limitations:**\n\nSome parameters influence the initialization of some data structures and cannot be changed when optimization is already in progress, such as PoolSearchMode or PoolSolutions.\n\nNote: The search results don't contain specific information about \"GAP_TIGHTEN\" as a parameter. This may be a feature in a newer version of Gurobi or a different naming convention. If you're looking for dynamic gap adjustment strategies, you may want to consult the latest Gurobi documentation or refer to parameters like `ImproveStartGap` which allows transitioning strategies based on reaching a target optimality gap.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a4ffb7c4-a658-488b-b3bb-1cb4bb0c812a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:16.159Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6df129ad-bd7a-41d2-a9a2-0cd6146337f2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
