{"parentUuid":"a8468b74-a456-4236-b796-a4749d580b71","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a0ac44e2d03f4edb2","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_015FjgHkNnaPzs5tgwScjAgo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HaHA68NhqdYenHxfwqxNr4","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"solver \"time budget\" allocation phase optimality proof tail \"primal-dual gap\" diminishing returns"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2912,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2040,"cache_read_input_tokens":31870,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2040,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011Caox9NJjCY3gRvoDPaeJ2","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"963200fa-c046-4725-bbba-5dcfd728a144","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:39.741Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a8468b74-a456-4236-b796-a4749d580b71","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a0ac44e2d03f4edb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GyjxibaTtuTjUnVGKXeEhz","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"CP-SAT\" continue solve previous model add constraint resume learned clauses persistent\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Modeling - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/04_modelling.html\"},{\"title\":\"A practical introduction to Constraint Programming using CP-SAT and Python\",\"url\":\"https://pganalyze.com/blog/a-practical-introduction-to-constraint-programming-using-cp-sat\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"🎓 How the CP-SAT solver works | Just another developer\",\"url\":\"https://xiang.es/posts/explaining-cp-sat/\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Constraint Programming Solver | google/or-tools | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/google/or-tools/4.1-cp-sat-constraint-programming-solver\"},{\"title\":\"Enhancing Hybrid CP-SAT Search for Disjunctive Scheduling\",\"url\":\"https://hal.science/hal-04174800/document\"}]\n\nI found relevant information about CP-SAT and its handling of learned clauses. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Learned Clauses in CP-SAT\n\nOver the course of solving, the solver might learn thousands or millions of clauses. This accumulated knowledge makes the solver progressively smarter.\n\n## Persistence of Learned Knowledge Across Restarts\n\nRestarts sound wasteful (throwing away all that search work), but they're surprisingly effective because the solver retains all learned clauses. The learned knowledge ensures restarting doesn't waste the work already done. Instead, restarting with accumulated learned clauses often finds solutions much faster than continuing down an unpromising search path.\n\n## Adding Constraints to Existing Models\n\nNew variables and new constraints can be added after the existing ones. This indicates that CP-SAT supports modifying models by adding additional constraints.\n\n## Core Mechanism\n\nThe foundation of CP-SAT is a CDCL (Conflict-Driven Clause Learning) SAT solver that works with Boolean variables and clauses. This core is extended to handle integer variables and complex constraints through a technique called \"lazy clause generation.\"\n\nIn essence, CP-SAT's architecture allows for continuing to solve previous models with added constraints while retaining learned clauses—the solver preserves the knowledge gained from earlier solving attempts and can reuse this learning when constraints are added and solving resumes.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"521f48c4-b8b9-47ed-9b2c-a24bbfcee054","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:45.391Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a8468b74-a456-4236-b796-a4749d580b71","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"963200fa-c046-4725-bbba-5dcfd728a144","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"4909c7d4-ca8e-4ff0-8bce-62f66c25edae","agentId":"a0ac44e2d03f4edb2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HaHA68NhqdYenHxfwqxNr4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"solver \"time budget\" allocation phase optimality proof tail \"primal-dual gap\" diminishing returns\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Optimising Budget Management via Primal-Dual Approximation\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3711896.3737071\"},{\"title\":\"What is the MIPGap? – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/8265539575953-What-is-the-MIPGap\"},{\"title\":\"An optimal first-order primal-dual gap reduction framework ...\",\"url\":\"https://optimization-online.org/wp-content/uploads/2015/10/5171.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"C H A P T E R 4 THE PRIMAL-DUAL METHOD FOR APPROXIMATION ALGORITHMS AND\",\"url\":\"https://math.mit.edu/~goemans/PAPERS/book-ch4.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Online Resource Allocation without Re-solving: The Effectiveness of Primal-Dual Policies by Siqi He, Yehua Wei, Jiaming Xu, Sophie H. Yu :: SSRN\",\"url\":\"https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=5133857\"},{\"title\":\"Optimising Budget Management via Primal-Dual Approximation with Constrained Polynomial Weights Update | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/394261635_Optimising_Budget_Management_via_Primal-Dual_Approximation_with_Constrained_Polynomial_Weights_Update\"},{\"title\":\"Duality gap - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duality_gap\"},{\"title\":\"Practical Large-Scale Linear Programming using Primal-Dual Hybrid Gradient\",\"url\":\"https://papers.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2021/file/a8fbbd3b11424ce032ba813493d95ad7-Paper.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Duality (optimization) - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duality_(optimization)\"},{\"title\":\"Competitive online algorithms for resource allocation over ...\",\"url\":\"https://par.nsf.gov/servlets/purl/10067675\"}]\n\nI found several relevant research papers and resources related to your search query. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Budget Management and Allocation\n\nA primal-dual approximation framework initializes the environment with computed anticipated budget utilization, which is used to allocate arriving impressions through refined primal-dual approximation, following which quantities and quality scores are updated along with pacing multipliers before proceeding to the next iteration.\n\n## Primal-Dual Gap and Optimality\n\nThe duality gap in optimization is the difference between the primal and dual solutions. The duality gap is zero if and only if strong duality holds. In the computational context, duality gap is part of the optimality criteria alongside primal feasibility and dual feasibility.\n\n## Diminishing Returns and Resource Allocation\n\nSmaller gaps in optimization lead to marginal solution improvements but require exponentially more effort. This demonstrates the diminishing returns principle in solver time allocation. The PSD diminishing returns (PSD-DR) property is used to relate sequential and simultaneous algorithm duality gaps to the dual optimal value.\n\n## Online Resource Allocation\n\nIn online resource allocation problems where requests arrive sequentially over time and must be served immediately under resource constraints, a primal-dual policy can solve the fluid linear program only once upfront and then use dynamic dual variable updates to reflect real-time resource availability.\n\nThe search results show active research in combining time budget allocation phases with primal-dual optimization methods, particularly in the contexts of advertising budget management and online resource allocation problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"1d7db633-119c-4cda-80f2-9cf741e994b8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:53:47.239Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"963200fa-c046-4725-bbba-5dcfd728a144","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"1d7db633-119c-4cda-80f2-9cf741e994b8","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a0ac44e2d03f4edb2","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01EdG52crR4EPRd5jYQvnEjm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"信息够，开始整合输出。\n\n---\n\n# ε-Gap 渐进收紧：从 5% → 1% → 0% 的工程落地方案\n\n## 核心结论（先说要点）\n\n**CP-SAT 和 Gurobi 都不支持\"原地\"动态收紧 gap**——参数在求解过程中是冻结的。所以\"渐进\"的工程实现是 **Stop → Reconfigure → Restart with Hint** 的三阶段流水线，靠 `add_hint(...)` + `repair_hint=True` 把上一阶段的 incumbent 喂给下一阶段，让新一轮搜索从已知好解开始往 proof 推。\n\nCP-SAT 的关键事实：\n- 重启不是\"续跑\"——learned clauses 和 dual bound 都会丢，但 SAT 内核本来就大量用 random restart，所以这个损失比看起来小，实际靠 hint 能很快回到 incumbent。\n- `add_hint` 是 phase saving，**不是硬约束**；可以喂部分变量也行（CP-SAT 偏好全量 hint）。\n- `repair_hint=True` + `hint_conflict_limit=20` 是 CPSAT-Primer 推荐的 daily replanning 标配。\n\nGurobi 的关键事实：\n- `ImproveStartGap` / `ImproveStartTime` 是内置的\"两段式\"——到了某个阈值就放弃 bound 转去刷 incumbent。**这是反向用法**，不是收紧 gap，而是放弃 proof。\n- 真正的\"收紧\"得在 callback 里 `model.terminate()`，外面改参数后 `optimize()` 续跑（同一个 model 对象会保留 cuts 和 node 树，**这是 Gurobi 比 CP-SAT 强的地方**）。\n\n## 三阶段配置模板（针对 70×70 + 266 实例）\n\n### Stage 1: Discovery（5% gap，预算 10 min，目标=找 incumbent）\n\n```python\nsolver.parameters.relative_gap_limit = 0.05\nsolver.parameters.max_time_in_seconds = 600\nsolver.parameters.num_workers = 8           # 多 worker 触发 LNS portfolio\nsolver.parameters.log_search_progress = True\n# 不喂 hint（首次跑）\nstatus = solver.Solve(model)\nincumbent = extract_solution(solver)        # 必须在 OPTIMAL/FEASIBLE 时存\nbest_bound_s1 = solver.BestObjectiveBound()\n```\n\n退化处理：10 min 内连 FEASIBLE 都没拿到 → 跳过 Stage 2，直接进 Stage 3 dump 一份 INFEASIBLE_OR_TIMEOUT 工件，外层降级到 exploratory cap 做兜底。\n\n### Stage 2: Refinement（1% gap，预算 1 h，从 S1 incumbent warm start）\n\n```python\n# 重新构建 model（结构相同），把 S1 解作为 hint\nfor var, val in incumbent.items():\n    model.add_hint(var, val)\n\nsolver.parameters.relative_gap_limit = 0.01\nsolver.parameters.max_time_in_seconds = 3600\nsolver.parameters.repair_hint = True\nsolver.parameters.hint_conflict_limit = 20\nsolver.parameters.num_workers = 8\n# 关键加速：把 S1 的 best_bound 作为 cut 喂进去\nmodel.add(objective_var >= int(best_bound_s1))   # 把 dual bound 显式化为约束\n```\n\n**bound transfer 是渐进收紧的灵魂**：S1 跑完得到 `(incumbent_value, best_bound)`，下一阶段把 `best_bound` 转成 `objective >= best_bound` 约束，这样 S2 不用再重新探一遍上界。这个技巧在 LBBD（你们已经在用）和 column generation 里都是标准做法。\n\n### Stage 3: Proof（0% gap，无预算/夜跑，certified_exact）\n\n```python\nfor var, val in s2_incumbent.items():\n    model.add_hint(var, val)\nmodel.add(objective_var >= int(best_bound_s2))\n\nsolver.parameters.relative_gap_limit = 0.0\nsolver.parameters.absolute_gap_limit = 0.0\nsolver.parameters.max_time_in_seconds = 86400 * 7    # 一周硬上限兜底\nsolver.parameters.num_workers = 16\nsolver.parameters.repair_hint = True\n# 关闭 LNS 偏好，转去做 proof\nsolver.parameters.use_lns_only = False\nstatus = solver.Solve(model)\nassert status == cp_model.OPTIMAL    # 只有这个才能写 certified_exact 工件\n```\n\n## 关键工业实例\n\n1. **Rolling-horizon scheduling** 是行业最常见的渐进收紧场景：CPLEX/Gurobi 跑 1h 拿到 0.3%（确定型）/ 1%（随机型）gap，然后下一个时间窗用上一窗的解 warm start。文献里很多用 15% gap 跑子问题再 aggregate。\n2. **Gurobi 官方推荐两段式**：`MIPFocus=3` 先冲 bound，到 `ImproveStartGap` 后切到 `MIPFocus=1` 刷 incumbent。\n3. **CP-SAT routing 团队**（Google 内部）报告 `routing_path_lns` 在 65 次调用里 41 次改进 incumbent——LNS 本身就是 anytime，是 5%→1% 这一段的主力。\n4. **ε-Constraint method**（多目标领域）：每轮把上轮 obj 转 ε-约束，跟你们要做的事数学上同构。\n\n## 学术名称\n\n学术圈这事儿叫 **anytime ε-tightening** 或 **target-gap scheduling**，跟 IDA*/RBFS 的 progressive deepening 不完全是一回事（后者收紧的是 depth bound 不是 ε）。比较接近的是 **bound-and-bound 的 dovetailing**，以及多目标 anytime 算法里的 ε-indicator 收敛。\n\n## 我们项目的实施计划\n\n**工程量评估（按你们 Phase 3B 的 lane 划分）：**\n\n| 模块 | 改动点 | 工程量 |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/search/exact_campaign.py` | 加 `stage_progressive` 字段记录 (5%, 1%, 0%) 三段进度，每段独立 checkpoint | 0.5 day |\n| `src/models/master_model.py` | 暴露 `objective_var` 和 `extract_hint(solution)` 接口 | 0.5 day |\n| 新建 `src/search/progressive_loop.py` | 三阶段 driver：Stage1 → 提取 incumbent + bound → 注入下一段 hint + bound cut → Stage2 → ... | 1.5 day |\n| `rules/progressive_schema.json` | 新增 schema：`{stage: 1/2/3, gap_target, gap_achieved, certified: bool}`；只有 stage=3 且 gap=0 才写 certified_exact | 0.5 day |\n| `src/tests/test_progressive_tightening.py` | mini 案例（10×10 + 5 实例）测三段都收敛 + bound 单调 | 1 day |\n| 与现有 Benders 集成 | 每次 Benders master 调用都套渐进收紧；最初只在 outer loop 的关键候选上启用，避免每个 candidate 都跑一周 | 1 day |\n\n**总计 5 天工程，预期收益 1000× 量级（来自之前 Round 3 调研）。**\n\n**与 PROJECT_LOCK 兼容：** Stage 1/2 的工件落到 `data/exploratory/progressive/stage{1,2}/`，明确标 `certified=false`；Stage 3 OPTIMAL 后才能写 `data/checkpoints/` 和 `data/solutions/`。schema 里 `stage` 和 `gap_achieved` 是 first-class 字段，AI sidecar 可以读但不能写（符合 AI Safety Contract）。\n\n**触发条件：** outer search 里只有当某 candidate 的 LB/UB 已经差不多收敛时才进 Stage 3，否则停在 Stage 2 的 1% gap。这就把 168h 总预算花在最有希望的少数 candidate 的 proof 上，而不是 wide proof 所有 candidate。\n\n## Sources\n\n- [CP-SAT Primer: Parameters](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html)\n- [CP-SAT Primer: Coding Patterns](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html)\n- [CP-SAT Primer: Large Neighborhood Search](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/09_lns.html)\n- [CP-SAT Primer: How does it work?](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html)\n- [Gurobi: What is the MIPGap?](https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/8265539575953-What-is-the-MIPGap)\n- [Gurobi: ImproveStartGap / ImproveStartNodes / ImproveStartTime](https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/5588450672529-Change-solution-strategy-to-standard-ImproveStartGap-ImproveStartNodes-ImproveStartTime)\n- [Gurobi: How do I change parameters in a callback?](https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/articles/360039233191-How-do-I-change-parameters-in-a-callback)\n- [Effective anytime algorithm for multiobjective combinatorial optimization (arXiv 2403.08807)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2403.08807)\n- [Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search for MIP (Springer)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12532-021-00209-7)\n- [Rolling Horizon MIP for Production Scheduling (Springer)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10100-023-00891-z)\n- [CP-SAT, UNKNOWN status with complete solution hint (or-tools issue #3750)](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5800,"cache_read_input_tokens":33910,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5800,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxAUiUQ8ExinNb9Noo3","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b3fdc521-086f-4e0b-8ffd-d59d5b00ea8b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T21:54:51.114Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
